  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["D9", "D10"],
      "pins": ["U11.6", "U11.7", "U10.6", "U10.7"],
      "nets": ["CAN0_P", "CAN0_N", "CAN1_P", "CAN1_N"],
      "observed": "On the CAN BUS sheets, references D9 and D10 are drawn as optocouplers (Input/Output symbols with LED+phototransistor pairs) placed in series between the isolated CAN transceivers U10/U11 (pins 6/7, CANH/CANL) and the CAN0_P/CAN0_N and CAN1_P/CAN1_N nets that run to connectors J2/J13. No CDSOT23-SM712 TVS diode array appears anywhere on the CAN lines.",
      "expected": "The specification states D9 and D10 are 'CDSOT23-SM712 TVS diode arrays on CAN0_P/N, CAN1_P/N' providing 'CAN bus transient/ESD protection', matching the documented part family 'SM712-TP or SM712-02HTG', and that the CAN controllers drive the buses 'through an isolated CAN transceiver (U11/companion)' directly to J2/J13.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "D9, D10 — CDSOT23-SM712 TVS diode arrays on CAN0_P/N, CAN1_P/N | CAN bus transient/ESD protection | docs/twistedfields-notes.txt lists 'TVS Diodes: SM712-TP or SM712-02HTG' as the intended part family for this role; the netlist's CDSOT23-SM712 matches this documented choice."},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "CAN BUS sheet: U11 pins 6/7 (CANH/CANL) feed 'Input' of D10, whose 'Output' pins drive CAN0_P/CAN0_N to J2; U10 pins 6/7 feed 'Input' of D9, whose 'Output' pins drive CAN1_P/CAN1_N to J13. D9/D10 are drawn as optocouplers, not TVS arrays; no SM712 part is present on either CAN net."}
      ],
      "impact": "The specified transient/ESD protection on both CAN buses is missing, and the differential CAN signals are instead routed through series optocouplers, which cannot faithfully carry 1 Mbps CAN data. Communication with the Odrive motor controllers on CAN0/CAN1 would fail or be unreliable, and the M12 connectors are exposed to ESD/transients.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The CAN interface deviates from the specified design: references D9/D10, which the spec documents as CDSOT23-SM712 TVS arrays protecting CAN0_P/N and CAN1_P/N, are instead implemented as optocouplers inserted between the isolated transceivers U10/U11 and the CAN connectors, leaving the buses without their specified ESD/transient protection and putting optocouplers in series with the CAN signaling path."
}

